From f06f975877bf592b9ac61b14ab11daa6ac2aabd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Gre=C5=84?= <witold.gren@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:06:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] talk: feed the camera's speaker in real time

A live talk waited for the camera's answer to each ADPCM block (64 ms of sound) before sending
the next one. Over a 4G relay that round trip is longer than the block, so the sound reached the
camera slower than it was spoken: the talker's queue (30 blocks) filled, the voice lagged more
and more and was cut where the queue overflowed.

The live talk (WebSocket /talk) now uses BcCamera::talk_live: the blocks come over a tokio
channel and are sent as they come, the camera's answers are read beside the sending (no blocking
read inside the async task either), and the sending is only held back when it is more than
300 ms ahead of what the camera has played. The queue is 8 blocks (about half a second): when
the link stalls, new sound is dropped instead of being played late. talk_stream, used to play
files, is unchanged.
---
 crates/core/src/bc_protocol/talk.rs | 166 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/ws/talk.rs                      |  23 ++--
 2 files changed, 161 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

